.TH ZEX-HISTORY 1 "2026-07-19" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex-history \- show the unified install/remove/upgrade history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zex history
.RI [ \-\-package\ <name> ]
.RI [ \-n\ <count> ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zex history
prints a single, unified, cross-tier timeline of every install, remove,
and upgrade operation, most recent first.
.PP
It reads
.IR /var/lib/zex/history.json ,
a flat JSON log written to by
.BR zex-install (1),
.BR zex-remove (1),
and
.BR zex-upgrade (1)
(both
.B uland
and
.B syshub
modes) every time they complete an operation, whether it succeeded or
failed.
Each entry records the operation type, the affected package(s) and
version(s), success/failure, an error message on failure, how long the
operation took, and which user invoked it.
.PP
This complements, rather than replaces, the older tier-specific audit
logs
.RI ( upgrade\-audit.toml ", " remove\-audit.toml )
— those still exist per-subsystem; this is the one place that shows
everything together on one timeline.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-package\  name
Only show entries that touched the package
.IR name .
.TP
.BI \-n\  count \fR,\  \-\-limit\  count
Show at most
.I count
entries (default: 20). Applied after filtering by
.BR \-\-package .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Always, whether or not any history is recorded.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the last 20 operations across all packages:
.PP
.nf
    zex history
.fi
.PP
Show every recorded operation touching
.BR musl :
.PP
.nf
    zex history --package musl
.fi
.PP
Show only the last 5 operations:
.PP
.nf
    zex history -n 5
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/zex/history.json
The unified history log. A JSON array, capped at the most recent 1000
entries; older entries are pruned automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zex-install (1),
.BR zex-remove (1),
.BR zex-rollback (1)
